# ship-pr's build of the would-be merge commit (lukstafi/ludics-lite#611, landed by
# lukstafi/ludics-lite#630). `pr-review.sh merge` reads this file from master: when master has
# moved since the PR's merge base and a path BOTH sides changed is an input below, it builds the
# PR head merged with master's tip in a scratch repository, runs `command` at its root inside the
# box's run-time slot, and refuses the merge (exit 1, no waiver) when that fails. Without this
# file a merge builds nothing.
#
# Inputs -- the boundary. A path is an input when one glob matches the WHOLE repository path
# (fnmatch, case-sensitive, `*` crossing `/`); a shared path renamed on either side counts by its
# other name too. The one glob below makes EVERY path an input (gh-ocannl-1382): the command's
# compile tier runs `@test/operations/scans`, which read the repository itself -- Markdown notes
# and docs (agent_notes_structure, agents_md_size, doc_examples), goldens, workflow YAML, Python,
# scripts -- so a narrower list would be a second copy of the scans' corpora, stale the day a scan
# reads a new kind of file; the few paths nothing reads (editor settings) cost a build only when
# both sides change one. Replayed over the 474 first-parent merges on master from 2026-09-19 to
# 2026-10-19, the OCaml-and-scripts list this replaced built 166 of them, adding `*.md` would
# build 238 and every path builds 245, at about 40 s each. What stays outside: a clash across
# paths only ONE side changed, and one the compile tier cannot see (a runtime test's verdict);
# both are the integration loop's, on master.
#
# Trust. The command is this repository's own code, trusted as a developer's build is: the
# scratch repository is a place to build, not a sandbox. It runs from whatever environment
# `merge` has; tools/merge-build-check.sh states its tiers, what selects them, their measured
# cost and how it finds dune when that environment lacks the opam switch.
command tools/merge-build-check.sh
input *
timeout 1200
